 ### Time and Memory Complexity
-*   **Vertex Extraction:** The complexity is dominated by the number of normal triplets and the size of the offset vectors [S1]. For $N_n$ normals and average offset vector length $L$, the number of candidate vertices per triplet is $L^3$ [S1]. With $O(N_n^3)$ triplets, the total candidate count is $O(N_n^3 L^3)$ [S1]. However, the computation is highly parallelizable via tensor broadcasting [S1].
-*   **Edge Extraction:** The complexity depends on the number of normal pairs $O(N_n^2)$ and the number of offset pairs $O(L^2)$ [S1]. For each pair, vertices are filtered and sorted [S1]. Not given in the sources.
